WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.001 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-"Newlywed Kitchen."

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:03.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess I'm four years in now
to my marriage.

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:04.537 line:92%
Does this still work for me?

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:05.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, boy.
The recipes are so good.

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
What's difference --

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:09.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
What's the difference
between recipes for newlyweds

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:11.378
and people who have been married
for like 20 years?

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:14.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Chuckles ] Not much.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:14.748 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Not much.

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:16.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's just
a little more enthusiasm.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:18.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
You probably go into it
together and say,

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:19.753 line:92%
"We should cook together."

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:21.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Smaller amounts.
-Okay.

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:23.623
-And it's when you really
do want to cook together.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:27.227
And actually there's so many
great recipes in this book,

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:28.228 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and it's beautiful.

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:29.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, well, it's
a Martha Stewart book.

00:00:29.596 --> 00:00:31.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't think --
I'm cooking from it.

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:32.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Are you really?
-And I'm not a newlywed.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is interesting
that it's Game Day Chili,

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:37.270
because I think one half of
newlyweds don't love that.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.773
-[ Laughs ]
-But that's all right. Maybe --

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:43.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They don't like game day,
you mean? Yeah, right.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.144 line:92%
-So let me ask you about this.

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:46.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were up at 5:00 a.m.
this morning.

00:00:46.146 --> 00:00:47.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ugh!
-You went to your

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:49.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
granddaughter's school
to make cookies.

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:50.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did. I did.
-How'd it go?

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:53.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I had to
bake the cookies.

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:53.753 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Because they -- I was --

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:57.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
My job was to teach them
how to decorate gingerbread.

00:00:57.557 --> 00:00:58.124 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh. Got it.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:00.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So not a gingerbread house,
but gingerbread men.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:02.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
Gingerbread trees.
Gingerbread gnomes.

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:05.632 line:92%
And they had the greatest time.

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:07.567 line:92%
-That is -- Just be jealous

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:10.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
for not having a school
that --

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
There you go. That's a better
way of showing that.

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:12.605 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's better.

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, that looks
like an assembly line.

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:17.110
-And that's my little
granddaughter right over there.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:19.813
-Oh, that's fantastic.
-And she's like a little Martha.

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:20.647 line:92%
We call her Little Martha.

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:22.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, there you guys are,
hard at work.

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:23.450 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's fantastic.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:26.619 size:88% position:44%
-And she loves to help
and do all those things.

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:30.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha. And are -- are kids
in that -- at that age

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:31.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
intimidated when
Martha Stewart comes in?

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:34.094 size:88% position:44%
-No. They couldn't wait
to get to those cookies.

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:36.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
They couldn't wait
to get the pastry bags

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:39.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the tips and the spatulas
and everything.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:41.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How did they do? Be honest.
How did they do?

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Most of them were
very artistic, actually.

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:44.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that's good.
-And -- And I have --

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:47.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm gonna post some of their
pictures on my Instagram.

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:49.909
But they were very good cookies.
-All right.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. And some were
a little sloppy.

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:53.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the mess!
The mess afterward.

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.415 line:92%
Oh, yoy yoy. But it was --

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:58.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it was my fault
because I made the frosting

00:01:58.051 --> 00:02:00.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
a little too thin.
-Oh, okay.

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:01.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well I think
it's a big step forward

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:04.357
that you're finally taking blame
for mistakes like that.

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:06.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am. [ Laughs ]
I'm working on it.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:09.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I feel like that's good.
-I'm working on it.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:12.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you -- This is -- there's
no blame to be had here.

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:14.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
You hosted a holiday party.
-You didn't come.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I didn't come, but I --
-I invited you.

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:18.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, here's the thing.
I didn't know --

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:20.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wanted to see photos
of this year's

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:21.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
before I decided
about next year.

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:22.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-I mean, this is --

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:25.011
Is this actually the kitchen
during your holiday party?

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:26.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's my kitchen.
-I mean, look at that.

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We had four different
kinds of hams.

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:31.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Four different -- What are
the four kinds of ham?

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:32.285 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-We had an ibérico ham.

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:36.489 size:88% position:44%
We had a La Quercia ham
from the Midwest that --

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:38.791
They eat only acorns, the pigs.
-Oh, wow.

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.760 line:92%
-And it's such a delicious ham.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:41.928 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And we had a country ham

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:44.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the Loveless Motel
down in Nashville.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God.
-Have you ever had that?

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:47.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-Ah, the best.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.402
-And we had a Pat LaFrieda ham.
-That's fantastic.

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:50.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And they were all
cooked differently.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:54.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they were all gone.
I don't even have a ham bone.

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:56.409 line:92%
I don't know who took the bones.

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:58.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You didn't --
-I want the bones!

00:02:58.278 --> 00:02:59.579 line:92%
-Those ungrateful S.O.B.'s

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:01.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
didn't even leave you
the ham bone?!

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:04.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How many -- How many cookies
were at your party?

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:06.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We did -- I think --
My granddaughter told me

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:09.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was 1,001 cookies
that we made.

00:03:09.389 --> 00:03:10.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-And look how cute they are.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're really nice.
-Yeah, they're really cute.

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:14.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now be honest.
Would you have had

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
the fifth-grade cookies
here at this?

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:18.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-Yeah, okay, good.

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:20.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Jude's maybe. Jude's.
-Okay. Gotcha.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.304 size:81% position:41%
So, a couple questions
about holiday parties.

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:25.405 line:92%
Some Martha Stewart rules.

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:27.273
If you're going to a holiday
party, are you supposed to

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:29.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
bring something and
what's a good thing to bring?

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:31.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you don't
have to take anything.

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:32.712 line:92%
But -- Because my house --

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:34.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, you should see
my front hall.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:35.982 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:37.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's like -- like --
so many presents.

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:40.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm kind of embarrassed
because I don't need anything.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:41.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Well, that's the thing.
I would --

00:03:41.955 --> 00:03:44.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would feel so much pressure
trying to think of,

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:46.359 line:92%
what does Martha Stewart need

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:48.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
that she didn't go out
and get herself?

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:50.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no. I don't get things.
I'm not like that.

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:53.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not -- I'm not --
I don't have to get things.

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:56.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, they just show up.
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:03:56.536 --> 00:03:58.304 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:01.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I don't want to say
that you're just sitting here

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:03.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
being inactive
and things are showing up.

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:04.344 line:92%
Because you did something

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:06.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I would not do
and I am so impressed.

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:08.648 line:92%
You plow your own driveway.

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:10.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do.
I have a four-mile driveway.

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:12.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I mean really, truly --

00:04:12.619 --> 00:04:14.621
I live on a farm,
so there's four miles of roads.

00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:18.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I actually love --
It's like flying an airplane.

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:20.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you get into a truck
with a plow,

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:22.195 line:92%
you can't think of anything else

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:24.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause, you know,
can't go off the road.

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:25.632 size:81% position:41% line:92%
You'll hit the stakes.

00:04:25.632 --> 00:04:27.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you don't want
to hit anything.

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:29.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you're dialed in.
-I'm dialed in.

00:04:29.369 --> 00:04:30.670 line:92%
And I just plow for like --

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
Four hours it takes to do --
-No! Four hours?

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:34.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It does. Because
you have to go one way

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:36.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then you have to
come back the other way.

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:39.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So two hours each way.
-Yes.

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:41.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But you got stuck.
This is an Instagram.

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:42.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
You said, "I went to plow,
and I got stuck."

00:04:42.649 --> 00:04:45.585
-Then I had to get pulled out by
the Kawasaki or whatever we had.

00:04:45.585 --> 00:04:49.289 size:84% position:42%
-Now, yeah, so, are you
embarrassed when you --

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:50.423 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Does panic set in?

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:51.824 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-No! No, it's natural.

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:53.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It's one of those things.

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:55.094 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's not natural.

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:58.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-This is a manmade machine.

00:04:58.331 --> 00:05:00.733
That's not --
-No, it's natural to get stuck.

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:02.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it is natural
to get stuck.

00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:05.104 size:81% position:41%
-I mean, my plow guys,
they don't get stuck.

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:07.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
How do your plow guys feel

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:09.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the fact that you're
doing it by yourself?

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:11.878
-They're happy, probably,
because they're inside

00:05:11.878 --> 00:05:14.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
drinking hot coffee
while I'm out

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:15.381 line:92%
plowing in the freezing cold.

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:17.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What's your -- What's --
We're gonna make some drinks,

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:18.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
some holiday drinks
just in a second.

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.553
-Oh, I can't wait. I can't wait.
-Do you have a favorite?

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:21.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, let's --
We'll wait and talk about --

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:24.390
-One of the drinks has cachaca,
which is my favorite.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:25.458 line:92%
-Cachaca? What's cachaca?

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:26.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's that
Brazilian cane liqueur.

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:29.162
-You have a favorite liquor
that's a Brazilian cane liquor?

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:32.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep.
-You are living the best life.

